---
// Move 1. States the problem and points at the one thing that is real and
// shipping today: the benchmark. The pull-request verifier is a labelled
// waitlist further down the page. The live command line is chrome, like the
// status bar: the one string on the page that is not site copy.
---

<section class="section-hero">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="hd reveal">Independent verification for AI-authored code</p>

    <p class="prompt reveal mt-7" style="--reveal-delay:40ms" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="c">$</span> assay verify ./patch.diff <span class="cursor"></span>
    </p>

    <h1 class="h1 reveal mt-7" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
      Verify <span class="g">AI-authored</span> fixes
    </h1>

    <p class="lede reveal mt-8" style="--reveal-delay:90ms">
      <b>Your AI fixed it. We check whether it actually did.</b>
    </p>

    <p class="lede reveal mt-4" style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
      AI writes your security fixes now, and most of them work. The dangerous one closes the
      hole and quietly breaks something your tests never checked. Assay catches it.
    </p>

    <div class="reveal mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3" style="--reveal-delay:180ms">
      <a href="/benchmark" class="btn btn-primary">Run the benchmark</a>
      <a href="/the-index" class="btn btn-secondary">Read the Index &rarr;</a>
    </div>

    <p class="disc reveal mt-8" style="--reveal-delay:240ms">
      Free and open &middot; Four SQL injection flaws &middot; Bring any fixer
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
